<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales remain slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales remain slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat prices were mostly marked higher in line with gains in MGE futures Monday in very subdued conditions.</p>
<p>Dealers said export demand was currently sluggish and producer selling remained slow with the bullish mood among farmers spreading from soybeans and corn to wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;Wheat is not bullish but the farmers are,&quot; one dealer said, noting he did not believe the farmers bullish mood was justified based on market fundamentals.</p>
<p>MGE May futures closed 5-1/4 cents higher at $4.00-1/4.  </p>
